    "title": "Compiler ICEs in CI?",
    "body": "Looks like there are a bunch of GCC 12 ICEs in the Warp CI:\n\n* Task previous releases: https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/actions/runs/32101345101/job/95602400388\nLLM reason (✨ experimental): CI failed due to a GCC 12 internal compiler error (segmentation fault) while compiling src/rpc/blockchain.cpp.\n\n* Task previous releases: https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/actions/runs/33372693809/job/99427161856\nLLM reason (✨ experimental): CI failed due to a GCC 12 internal compiler error (segmentation fault) while compiling txmempool/tinyformat.h during the build.\n\nNot sure why they would pop up now, when they never happened before?",
